{
    "background_story": "Prince was a majestic stallion, known for his striking coat and regal demeanor. But beneath his proud exterior, Prince had been struggling with a severe infection that had left him weakened and in pain. His owner, a kind old veterinarian, had tried various treatments to no avail. Just when all hope seemed lost, she discovered that Prince was a rare case requiring a specific antibiotic - cefotaxime. Administered promptly, the medication worked wonders, and Prince began to recover. As he regained his strength, Prince's loyalty and affection for his owner only deepened. He would follow her everywhere, nuzzling her gently and whinnying softly. The veterinarian credited cefotaxime with saving Prince's life, and the horse became a living testament to the power of modern medicine and the unbreakable bond between humans and animals.",
